  "comment": "The opkg utility (an ipkg fork) is a lightweight package manager used to download and install OpenWrt packages from local package repositories or ones located in the Internet. GNU/Linux users already familiar with apt-get, aptitude, pacman, yum, etc. will recognize the similarities. Opkg attempts to resolve dependencies with packages in the repositories - if this fails, it will report an error,",
